  "limitations": [
    "108 named assertions per guest: 35 state lease, 28 ownership reads and 45 ACL assertions. Three native fixture tests, seven unit tests and 57 codec subtests execute without skips. Both UFS ACL models use only owned 32 MiB memory devices; native ZFS/UFS root lease/read tests also rerun.",
    "Actual opened descriptors use fpathconf capability queries. Two confirmed zeros establish mode-only access; unknown/error/conflicting answers deny without ENOTSUP fallback. Enabled ACLs use the fixed-width 4088-byte FreeBSD syscall ABI, no cgo or command executor in product code.",
    "Conservative allowlist, not general ACL equivalence: POSIX access contains only mode entries and defaults are empty. NFSv4 named principals, inheritance flags and nonowner grants outside mode data/search plus standard ancillary reads deny. Root-owner known rights and additional deny entries may be accepted. No xattr confidentiality or external client/share ACL claim.",
    "Actual UID/GID 65534 with no privileged groups can open/read an ACL-granted root-owned 0600 record under a root-owned 0700 directory through its inherited directory descriptor, while the product reader refuses that UID. The child is waited/reaped and its copied executable removed. Not a built product helper/executor qualification.",
    "Native named/inheritable directory/ancestor/lock/record refusals preserve fixture modes, UIDs, named inodes, ACLs and record bytes. Ancestor refusal creates no missing lock. Tests restore only owned ACL controls; product code never modifies ACLs or repairs permissions.",
    "Checks detect observed ordinary drift, not malicious root modification or a filesystem fence. Synchronized ACL/object replacement during reads, syscall errors, I/O deadlines and complete state provisioning remain unqualified.",
    "Prior manifests retain exact bytes/tested sources. This expanded state/codec suite reruns only its declared proofs; historical device/property suites are not relabeled.",
    "Owned mounts are unmounted, memory devices detached, child/descriptors/fixtures removed; host image/key/variables absent, base/runtime preserved, supervised groups stopped. No host mount/service/persistent runner. GitHub Actions remain disabled.",
    "Full store/enumeration budgets, atomic publication, job schemas/admission/reservations/history, read-only/full-store/sync/rename faults, acknowledgements, reboot/power-loss/metadata restore and M2 acceptance remain ahead. Missing slice 1 observations confer no authority. Runtime remains read-only; M1 Safari/manual accessibility remains pending.",
    "Final documentation-head review is separate and functional/test/tool inputs remain unchanged. Primary sources establish interface semantics, not installed binary build provenance. No hardware/controller/commercial support follows."
  ]
}
